  <conditions attached="1">
   <condition type="1">
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Consistent with the Article III of the SBAA [or the Supplemental Provisions to the Project Document], the responsibility for the safety and security of the Implementing Partner and its personnel and property, and of UNDP&#x2019;s property in the Implementing Partner&#x2019;s custody, rests with the Implementing Partner.  To this end, the Implementing Partner shall: a)	put in place an appropriate security plan and maintain the security plan, taking into account the security situation in the country where the project is being carried; b)	assume all risks and liabilities related to the Implementing Partner&#x2019;s security, and the full implementation of the security plan.</narrative>
   </condition>
   <condition type="1">
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Social and environmental sustainability will be enhanced through application of the UNDP Social and Environmental Standards (http://www.undp.org/ses) and related Accountability Mechanism (http://www.undp.org/secu-srm).</narrative>
   </condition>
  </conditions>
  <result aggregation-status="1" type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Annual Output Results</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator ascending="0" measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output Indicator</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Institutional  mechanism for SDGs Coordination  in place</narrative>
    </description>
    <baseline year="2018">
     <comment>
      <narrative xml:lang="EN">IInstitutional  mechanism for SDGs Coordination not in place</narrative>
     </comment>
    </baseline>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2020-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2020-12-31"></period-end>
     <target>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">1. Meetings of MKUZA III Steering Committee, ZJP Sub Committee as well as Technical Working Groups of MKUZA III M&amp;E Secretariat organised.

2. SDGs Roadmap developed.

3. SDGs and MKUZA III M&amp;E systems and tools developed.

4. Zanzibar taskforce members participate in the SDGs National Coordination Taskforce events. 

5. 2019/20 Annual SDGs Report produced.

6. Support data collection for 2019/20 HBS.

7. Enhanced ZPCs capacity in coordination, monitoring and reporting of SDGs. 

8. Government and private sector officials attend regional and international forums on SDGs.

9. National Strategy for Development of Statistics (NSDS) finalized.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">1. Consultative meetings organized for Senior Government Officials in Unguja and Pemba, to facilitate review and finalization of the Draft Evaluation Report of the Zanzibar Development Vision 2020 (ZDV 2020)

2. SDGs Roadmap developed.

3. SDGs and MKUZA III M&amp;E systems and tools developed. Can be accessed at http://www.zmes.planningznz.go.tz 

4.  2019/20 Annual SDGs Implementatio Report produced.

5. Supported  OCGS in data collection and production of 2019/20 HBS

6. .Enhanced ZPCs capacity in  coordination, monitoring and reporting of SDGs.

7. National Strategy for Development of Statistics (NSDS) drafted, awaiting govenments approval.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
    </period>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2021-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2021-12-31"></period-end>
     <target>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">1. Development and printing of the Zanzibar Monitoring and Evaluation Policy.
2. M&amp;E Staff trained on Project Coordination and Team Management Skills

3. Develop and Print popular versions of MKUZA III Evaluation report and 2019/20Annual SDGs Implementation Report . 

4. Equipment for the Monitoring and Evaluation system procured. 

5. Initiation plan for a successor project, developed.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">1. Draft Monitoring and Evaluation Policy in place
2. Eight (6 female &amp; 2 male ) are trained Project Coordination and Team Management Skills
3. Popular version of MKUZA III Evaluation report produced and ---copies printed
4. Equipment ( 5 computers, 3 laptops and 2 printers) were procuredfor the Monitoring and Evaluation system</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
    </period>
   </indicator>
